This crate (`symphonia-codec-atrac3plus`) is a from-scratch, pure-Rust ATRAC3+ decoder. It is
licensed under the Mozilla Public License, v. 2.0, like the rest of Project Symphonia.

ATRAC3+ has no public specification. The bitstream parser, the canonical Huffman codebook
descriptors and all other tables (`src/tables.rs`, extracted programmatically), the gain
compensation, power compensation ("noise dithering"), sine-wave (GHA) synthesis, IMDCT windowing and
inverse polyphase quadrature filter bank follow FFmpeg's `libavcodec/atrac3plusdec.c`,
`libavcodec/atrac3plus.c`, `libavcodec/atrac3plusdsp.c`, `libavcodec/atrac3plus_data.h` and
`libavcodec/atrac.c`, which are distributed under the GNU Lesser General Public License,
version 2.1 or later. The technical description at
http://wiki.multimedia.cx/index.php?title=ATRAC3plus was used by the FFmpeg authors.

